      "title": "Cong used banks as 'personal entities': Sitharaman amid IDBI divestment row",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/cong-used-banks-as-personal-entities-sitharaman-amid-idbi-divestment-row-126103000662_1.html",
      "description": "Amid the row over divestment of IDBI Bank, Finance Minister Nirmala Sitharaman on Friday took on the Congress party and the previous UPA government, alleging they used banks and financial institutions as \"personal entities\" and pressured bank employees to extend loans at their whim, bypassing prudent lending norms.\nIn a post on X, the Finance Minister also cited several instances from the Congress-led government, including the removal of SBI Chairman R K Talwar in 1976 under Indira Gandhi's rule after he allegedly refused to give in to political pressure to relax lending norms for a company linked to Sanjay Gandhi.\nShe was responding to a post on X by senior Congress leader Rahul Gandhi on IDBI Bank.\nOn the remarks made by Rahul Gandhi, Sitharaman said, \"IDBI Bank was handed over to us in poor shape, as IDBI itself was forced to lend to large business groups with close connections to @INCIndia leaders such as Videocon, Winsome, ABG Shipyard, and Kingfisher.\n\"These turned into bad .",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-30T08:33:28"
    },
    {
      "title": "Rahul Gandhi backs IDBI Bank staff, questions sale to Canada's Fairfax",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/politics/rahul-gandhi-backs-idbi-bank-staff-questions-sale-to-canada-s-fairfax-126103000285_1.html",
      "description": "Amid the IDBI bank disinvestment row, Congress leader Rahul Gandhi has expressed solidarity with the bank employees and questioned the government's decision to sell off the profitable public bank to a Canadian firm.\nThe Leader of Opposition in the Lok Sabha asserted that public banks are not assets to be sold off, they are tools to build the nation.\nIn a letter addressed to members of the IDBI Bank family, Gandhi said that in March last year, a group of IDBI bank employees came to meet him in Parliament House and asked him a simple question as to why the government is selling a bank that they had made profitable.\n\"I took that question to the Lok Sabha. I asked why a profitable public bank was being sold and how its employees and depositors would be protected. The government gave no reason. Now it has decided to sell IDBI Bank to Fairfax, a Canadian company,\" Gandhi said.\nNoting that IDBI began as a pioneering development bank, he said the journey to a commercial bank has been ...",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-30T04:51:40"
    },
    {
      "title": "Govt defends IDBI Bank valuation, says process added ₹3,917 cr to deal value",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/companies/news/idbi-bank-stake-sale-government-valuation-defends-bidding-process-deal-value-126103000338_1.html",
      "description": "The Finance Ministry said the Core Group of Secretaries on Disinvestment had the authority to decide the bidding process, which helped increase the IDBI Bank stake sale value by ₹3,917 crore",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-30T04:49:39"
    }
